    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that \"defiant spark\" feels so exhausting. like, if the end result is always zero, then any value we create is just a temporary glitch. it feels more rational to just accept the physics of it and stop fighting the current. why put in the work to maintain this complex state when the universe is literally designed to tear it down? it feels like we're just prolonging the discomfort.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
